### Command relationships
- **`pnpm run dev`** — after the first **`eleventy.after`** in **`--serve`**, config opens **`http://127.0.0.1:<port>/`** once (**`scheduleOpenDevBrowserOnce`** in **`eleventy/config/events.js`**): **`ELEVENTY_OPEN_BROWSER=0`** / **`false`** / **`no`** disables; **`ELEVENTY_DEV_SERVER_URL`** overrides when the dev server port differs from **`--port`**; skipped when **`CI`** is set or **`ELEVENTY_RUN_MODE`** is not **`serve`**.
- `deploy` runs: `changelog` → `generate-og-images` → `test markdown` → `test frontmatter` → `build` → `test og-images` → rsync → Cloudflare purge (content-hash diff) → IndexNow; if changelog changed, deploy then commits and pushes it (skipped with `--dry-run`). **Deploy output is quiet by default (2026-08-13)** — rsync argv is built by **`scripts/utils/deploy-rsync.js`**; **`--itemize-changes`** / **`--stats`** / **`--human-readable`** are added only for **`--verbose`** or **`--dry-run`**, and a quiet run withholds rsync's buffered stdout unless the exit code is non-zero (stderr always prints). Every build rewrites **`_site/`**, so itemize listed ~thousands of mtime-only lines each deploy and overflowed the terminal; nothing consumes that list anymore (purge diffs content hashes and prints its own counts, capped at 8 URLs). Don't "restore" itemize as the default — **`pnpm run test deploy-guards`** asserts the built argv per mode and will fail. **rsync** must not **`--exclude=color/`** — **`/color/`** is a normal output directory (an old exclude caused live **404** while **`/type/`** / **`/ogimages/`** still deployed). Optional **`CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID`** + **`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`** (Cache Purge); **`CLOUDFLARE_PURGE=0`** disables and must not write manifest. **`.htaccess`** sets CSS **`max-age=2592000`** (30d) — browser cache survives CF purge; selective purge fixes edge only. Manual CF purge: use **apex** `https://jonplummer.com/...` — `www` only **301**s; purging `www…/assets/*` leaves the apex CSS HIT intact. **Content-hash purge (2026-08)** — after rsync, SHA-256 walk of **`_site/`** vs **`.cache/deploy-content-manifest.json`** (purge list independent of rsync itemize); purge **`changed` ∪ `deleted`** only (skip **`added`** — new URLs never cached; same-path OG regen still **`changed`**); no baseline → skip purge, write manifest; **`CLOUDFLARE_PURGE_FORCE_CONTENT=1`** full content purge; purge fail/disabled → no manifest write. Helpers in **`scripts/utils/cloudflare-purge.js`**; **`pnpm run test cloudflare-purge`**. Later: reuse manifest for rsync volume — **`docs/ideas.md`** Future → Deploy / Cloudflare. **IndexNow rewrite (2026-08)** — replaced a git-diff-based detector (re-implemented Eleventy's permalink rules by hand, wrong; silently submitted 0 URLs on 16 of 18 deploys) with the same content-hash-manifest technique as Cloudflare purge, reusing `buildContentManifest`/`diffContentManifests`/`loadContentManifest`/`saveContentManifest`/`deployPathToUrl` from `cloudflare-purge.js` but with its **own** state file **`.cache/indexnow-content-manifest.json`** — must stay separate from Cloudflare's. **The two files are independent cursors, not redundancy (re-examined 2026-08-13)**: "last state submitted" vs "last state purged", each advancing only when its own consumer succeeds, and each consumer can be disabled alone (**`CLOUDFLARE_PURGE=0`**, missing **`INDEXNOW_API_KEY`**). Share one file and either one's failure or absence rewrites the other's retry state — with purging off nothing advances the cursor and IndexNow resubmits a growing set every deploy. The deploy-ordering argument (CF's manifest is saved before IndexNow runs, so a shared file diffs to zero) is true but only an artifact of where the write happens; don't rely on it as the reason. Only the **hash walk** is shared: **`deploy.js`** builds one manifest after rsync and passes it via **`currentManifest`** to both **`purgeChangedDeployContent`** and **`processIndexNow`** (each still loads/saves its own state file); **`processIndexNow`** also takes **`manifestPath`** for tests. Both unit tests prove injection by passing a nonexistent **`siteRoot`** (hashing it would throw). Guards: **`pnpm run test manifest-cursors`** runs deploy.js's composition against temp dirs with stubbed **`fetch`** (identical **`generatedAt`** in both files proves the shared walk; purge-off / purge-fail / IndexNow-fail prove cursor independence), and **`test deploy-guards`** counts **`buildContentManifest(`** call sites in deploy.js (must be **1**) and requires **`currentManifest`** in both call sites. Verified 2026-08-13 by mutation: pointing both cursors at one file fails 3 checks; dropping either **`currentManifest`** arg fails the guard. Real-deploy fingerprint: after a deploy on this code, **`generatedAt`** in the two `.cache` files must be an **identical string** (differing by ~0.5s means the old two-walk code ran). Submits `added ∪ changed` **`.html`** paths, excluding `404.html`/`500.html`/`page/N/index.html`; no previous manifest → establishes baseline, submits nothing (does not backfill). **Now runs during `--dry-run`** too (prints the would-submit list, does not POST or write state) — only the changelog commit/push remain dry-run-skipped. Missing `INDEXNOW_API_KEY` → warns and skips, never throws. **`pnpm run indexnow-catch-up`** (optionally `-- --dry-run`) submits every current indexable page regardless of manifest history — for clearing a backlog once, not part of normal deploys. Key rotation is now fully manual (doc-only, no script): new key string → `src/<key>.txt` + `.env` `INDEXNOW_API_KEY`; `keyLocation` is derived from the env var at request time. Unit: **`pnpm run test indexnow`** (fixture manifests, no network; one orchestration check uses a temp state file — moved out of `test fast`/`build.js` post-build into `test unit`).
- **Run timestamps (2026-08-13)** — **`build.js`** and **`deploy.js`** each end with **`🕒 <label> <clock> (<elapsed>)`** via **`scripts/utils/run-timing.js`** (**`formatClock`** / **`formatElapsed`** / **`formatRunFinishedLine`**). **Completion** time, not start — start is derivable from elapsed, and the question a scrolled-back terminal answers is "when did the site last go out?". Failure paths print **`Build failed`** / **`Deploy failed`** with the same shape; dry runs say **`Deploy (dry-run) finished`**. Deploy shells `pnpm run build`, so **two** 🕒 lines appear in a deploy (build's is a sub-total) — that's intended, not a duplicate. Elapsed rounds with a carry (**119.7s → `2m 0s`**, never `1m 60s`). No test entry — verified by running `build` + `deploy --dry-run`.
- **`import-links` NotePlan format** — NotePlan now stores notes as **`.md`** (legacy **`.txt`** still supported). **`findNotePlanNote`** recurses under **`Notes/`** (skips **`@Trash`** / **`@Archive`**) and matches title on first line or filename stem.
- **Test runner JSON IPC** — Child tests write `__TEST_JSON_START__`…`__TEST_JSON_END__` for the runner to format. **`outputResult`** uses **`writeSyncAll`** (loop until complete; optional **`stdout._handle.setBlocking(true)`**) — a single `fs.writeSync` to a non-blocking pipe returns after ~64KB and drops the rest (internal-links hit this; deploy aborted). Async `stdout.write` + `process.exit()` also truncates. Compact `JSON.stringify`. Guard fixture must be **>64KB**: **`pnpm run test test-json-pipe`** (in `test unit`).
- **Test manifest (2026-08)** — `scripts/test-manifest.js` is the single source of truth for test membership: `id` → script path + `groups` (`fast`/`pre`/`post`/`unit`/`changed`) + flags (`slow`/`nonJson`/`listInHelp`). `test-runner.js`, `build.js`, and `test-changed.js` all derive their lists from it (no more separate `testTypes`/`fastTests`/`PRE_BUILD_TESTS`/`CONTENT_CHANGED_TESTS` arrays); **`'all'` is derived as `'fast'` + `slow`-flagged tests**, not stored separately. Self-checks its own consistency on every `require()` (unknown script paths, `unit`/`fast` overlap, `changed` tests lacking real `--changed` support). **New test = one `TESTS` entry** with the right `groups` — no other file needs editing. `test fast` includes **`error-document-assets`** (404 root-absolute hrefs); `test all` adds `a11y`. **`test frontmatter`** parses **`src/_posts/*.md`** and **top-level `src/*.md`** with **gray-matter** (matches Eleventy); **`parseFrontMatter()`** in **`frontmatter-utils.js`** remains regex-based for scripts/tests that only need `---` … `---` splitting.
- Collected wisdom: `src/_data/wisdom-entries.yaml` + `wisdom.js` + `wisdom-build.js` + `wisdom-entries-path.js` (same folder as `links.yaml`; YAML basename ≠ `wisdom` so no merge clash with `wisdom.js`). Pagination needs `wisdom` in `getGlobalData()` — not `eleventyComputed` (runs too late). Pages `/wisdom/` and `/wisdom/tags/<tag>/`, RSS `/wisdom-feed.xml`, head link in `head/wisdom-feed.njk`; `markdown` filter renders block markdown from YAML; list UI uses `_includes/components/wisdom_entry.njk` (`footer` + `section`, same article grid as blog index; `article.wisdom-entry` skips the title row)
- `dev` auto-generates OG images on file save via `eleventy.beforeWatch`
- `validate` is shortcut for `test html`

### Workflow preferences
- **Stylelint**: `pnpm run lint:css` or `pnpm run test css`; config `.stylelintrc.json` (extends standard; several rules off for this stylesheet — see `docs/tests.md`). `scripts/test/css.js` uses `runTest`/`outputAndExit` like spell; maps Stylelint warnings to `line`/`column`/`ruleId`/`helpUrl` for `formatVerbose`. Included in `test fast`.
- **`test:changed` caveat**: `pnpm run test:changed` can report no markdown/YAML changes when edits are untracked (not yet committed), so run `pnpm run test fast` before committing new content files.
- **Color combo contrast badges**: `/color/` variant-combo cards (B&W/DR/wild/terminal) must update badge text/class on `<select>` change using per-variant `worstLcSrgb`/`worstLcP3`; static initial badge values can drift from the visible preview.
- **Harmony lab header badge**: **`renderHarmonyLabCard`** in **`generate-gallery.js`** — badge should state recipe count and that **L/C** come from the **APCA-tuned** export (≥ **`MIN_LC`** **Lc at build**); avoid vague “nudged build” alone (lede covers interactive controls).
- **Harmony lab (color-gallery)**: **Hue wheel disk** uses **`colorWheelDiskBackground()`** — **`oklch(L C Hdeg)`** conic (fixed L/C, **25** stops 0…360 in 15° steps) so disk angles match **OKLCH** marker dots and previews; an **`hsl()`** disk misaligns ~10–20° at the same nominal hue. Do not use only **`oklch(L C 0deg)` → `oklch(L C 360deg)`** without **`longer hue` / many stops**: browsers can take the **zero-length hue arc** and the ring looks **flat**. Markers are **white-filled** **`#fff`** with token-based outline shadow (no chroma fill); **`.color-wheel-dot--primary`** on hub / hue-preview; **`.color-wheel-dot--multi`** when harmony has **>3** distinct hues. **Hue wheel** `.color-wheel` must not use **`width: min(5.75rem, 100%)`** inside the embed **`hue-rotate-bar-grid` / `harmony-lab-top`** grid **`auto`** column — cyclic `%` makes intrinsic min-content **0** (wheel invisible). Use **`clamp(4rem, 28vw, 5.75rem)`** (or other definite lengths). Inline `linkDeltas` in `generate-gallery.js` must stay aligned with `buildHarmonySchemes` `pair(...)` offsets — recipe math is duplicated for the browser; **`markerHueDegrees`** (harmony hue-wheel dots) must stay aligned with the same **`linkDeltas`** cases. `tuningSlidersForRecipe` / `[data-harmony-tuning]` wrappers hide analogous / split / skew unless that recipe uses them. Harmony: **recipe** `<select>` uses **`aria-label`** only (no visible Recipe label). **Hue + tuning sliders** use visible **`<label for=…>`**. **`.harmony-lab-tuning-row[hidden]`** needs **`display: none !important`** so gallery `display:flex` does not defeat the **`hidden`** attribute. **`.harmony-lab-inline`** / **`.hue-rotate-inline`** use **`grid-template-columns: 1fr auto`** so range tracks share width. **`.harmony-lab-top`** is a **three-column** grid (**wheel · recipe · hue rotation**; collapses **42rem**). Hue reference: **`hue-rotate-bar-grid`** (**OKLCH conic** wheel + **`.hue-rotate-stack`**); wheel dot tracks **preview rotation** degrees (slider), not a single parsed theme hue.
- **Skewed split complementary tuning**: For `harmony-skewed-split-complementary`, `splitSpread (S)` controls arm separation and `harmonySkew (K)` shifts both arms together (`+hk` on both sides), not inward/outward (`+/-hk`). `K` is now treated as direct degrees (`hk = K`, no `/2`), so slider value matches perceived skew magnitude. Keep build-time `pair(...)` math and runtime `linkDeltas(...)` in sync.
- **Gallery caret sizing + token summary label**: In generated `color-gallery-embed.css`, shared details/summary carets (`.gallery-section-summary::before` + `.tokens summary::before`) use **`--icon-disclosure-caret-mask`** geometry (filled right triangle, path centered for centroid pivot — keep generator path in sync with `jonplummer.css`). Whole-pixel box **`10px × 10px`**, `transform-origin: 50% 50%`. Token disclosure summary text in the embed is **`View CSS tokens`**.
- **CSS token preview wrapping**: `.color-gallery-embed .code` now wraps long token lines (`white-space: pre-wrap` + `overflow-wrap: anywhere`) so the View CSS tokens panel is readable without horizontal scrolling.
