### Gotchas

- **Favicon on other sites (2026-08-23)** — `icon.svg` themes with `prefers-color-scheme` for **this** site’s tab. Scrapers copy rasters into `<img>` (`/fav/jonplummer.com`). Those rasters are plated: `favicon.ico` (32 + 256 PNG frames) and `apple-touch-icon.png` (180) from `icon-raster.svg` (dark mark `#2a2d32` on `#fafafa`). Not linked in HTML. Regen: **`pnpm run generate-favicon-rasters`**. Guard: **`pnpm run test favicon-rasters`**. Do not plate `icon.svg`.
- **cspell dictionary inflections** — a listed plural does not cover the singular (`touchpoints` was in `cspell-custom-words.txt`, `touchpoint` still flagged). Add each form that appears. Possessives (`Munroe's`) are checked as the whole token.
- **cspell skips image alt text** — `ignoreRegExpList` treats `![alt](url)` like a markdown link, so typos in alt text (`enoguh`, `knowedge`) never flag. Read alts when spell-checking a post.
- **Content dashes** — Prefer **en dash** (`–`) in posts/pages/links/wisdom, not em (`—`). Spaced parentheticals use ` – `; unspaced `word—word` becomes `word – word`. Inside `*emphasis*`, don’t put a space after the opening `*` (MD037) — attributions like `*– Name*` are fine. Name redaction: escape underscores (`M\_`) or use another mark; bare `M_ … D_` is parsed as emphasis.
- **`test frontmatter`** validates **top-level `src/*.md`** (not only **`_posts/`**). Malformed **`## title:`** or a missing closing **`---`** breaks gray-matter/Eleventy; **`404.md`** / **`500.md`** omit **`date`** (test allows that).
- **`body > main`** already sets **`max-width: var(--max-width)`** and **`padding: var(--gutter)`** — inner wrappers on utility pages (e.g. **`.type-tool-page`**, **`.preview-container`**) should not repeat horizontal gutter + max-width or content looks narrower than **`/changelog/`** / **`/technologies/`**. **`/type/`** font card: avoid extra horizontal **`padding`** on **`.font-tool-card`** / **`.tool-controls`** so text lines up with the page **`h1`** like **`/color/`**.
- **`/type/`**, **`/color/`**, **`/ogimages/`** use **`tags: page`** without **`eleventyExcludeFromCollections`** (same as **`/changelog`** / **`/technologies`**) — in **`collections.page`** and **`sitemap.xml`**; **`/feed.xml`** still posts-only. **`scripts/test/seo-meta.js`** **`EXCLUDED_SHORT_TITLES`** includes **`/type`**, **`/color`**, and **`/ogimages`** for intentional short slash **`<title>`** text like **`/changelog`**.
- **Color gallery embed + watch** — **`runColorGalleryBuild({ stableWildThemes: true })`** from **`eleventy.before`** (see **`eleventy/config/events.js`**): wild pack used **`Math.random`** so **`writeTextFileIfChanged`** rewrote **`color-gallery-embed-inner.html`** every build → Eleventy **`--watch`** loop. **`createStableRng`** + **`stableWildThemes`** fixes that; **`pnpm run color-gallery`** CLI still uses **`mathRnd`** for varied wild output.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files have YAML frontmatter (globs, alwaysApply) that Claude Code ignores — content is still valid markdown after the frontmatter
- **Portfolio import**: `pnpm run convert-presentation` (PDF + `.pptx` → notes via `extract-pptx-notes.py` + python-pptx); one-time **`pnpm run setup-deck-python`** (venv at `scripts/content/.venv/` — avoids Homebrew PEP 668 pip errors); `convert-pdf-with-notes` for hand-authored notes. See `docs/commands.md` § PDF page conversion; `docs/authoring.md` § Converting a PDF.
- **Date handling is load-bearing** — `addDateParsing` (timezone-aware) + permalink generation preserve WordPress-era URLs. Do not simplify without verifying every URL remains unchanged.
- Figure captions use the convention: image line immediately followed by `*caption text*` (no blank line). The `markdown-it-figure` plugin in `eleventy/utils/markdown-it-figure.js` handles this at parse time.
- **Post iframe demos** — Passthrough under **`src/assets/demos/<slug>/`** (`index.html` + same-origin **`*.js`** if interactive; production **`script-src 'self'`** blocks inline script even inside iframe documents). Use **`…/index.html`** in iframe `src` and pop-out links — Eleventy **`--serve`** passthrough does not resolve trailing-slash directory URLs to `index.html` (Apache DirectoryIndex may on production). Post embed: **`.post-demo-popout`** paragraph with unclassed **`a`** (underline via **`article a`**), **`.post-demo-embed`** iframe wrapper; **`.post-demo-embed-frame`** uses fixed **`height: 42rem`** (not `70vh`) so the crop fits controls + favorite + peek of next card — revisit per-demo heights if more demos land.
- Redirects: add entries to `src/_data/redirects.yaml` — the `src/.htaccess.njk` template renders them as Apache `Redirect 301` (prefix match). A slashed `from` (`/uses/`) does not match the bare path (`/uses`) when no directory exists (DirectorySlash never fires). Add both; list the slashed form **first** so the shorter prefix does not turn `/uses/` into `/technologies//`. No separate script needed.
- **`/technologies/` is not a `/uses` page** — it's a generated site-stack list (Eleventy, Node, tests), not hardware/editor/desk. `/uses/` 301s there for URL convention only. Don't submit to [wesbos/awesome-uses](https://github.com/wesbos/awesome-uses) unless there is an actual uses page (decided against 2026-08-23).
- **Eleventy image transform wraps `<img>` in `<picture>`** — when a parent element becomes a CSS grid container, `<picture>` is the grid item, not `<img>`. Target `> picture` for grid placement (e.g., `grid-column: 1 / -1`).
- **Spaces in asset filenames** break markdown link parsing (markdown-it doesn't recognize them as URLs) AND the Eleventy dev server's passthrough mode. Use kebab-case for all asset filenames.
- **Dark mode uses `light-dark()`** — colors are defined once in `:root` with `light-dark(lightVal, darkVal)`. Don't add a separate `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` block; add new colors using the same pattern.
- **`scripts/test/color-contrast.js` parses `:root` `light-dark()`** — raw hex or `oklch(...)`; **`scripts/utils/apca-dual.js`** computes Lc on **sRGB** and **Display P3** gamut maps (`sRGBtoY` / `displayP3toY`). **Pass/fail** uses sRGB only; warnings for P3 below min while sRGB passes or ΔLc≥4 while sRGB≥min. Gallery **`themes.json`**: **`worstLcSrgb`** / **`worstLcP3`**. Extend parsing if new color syntax appears in `jonplummer.css`.
- **`docs/archive/accessibility-test-limitations.md` is historical** — a11y (`accessibility.js`) disables axe `color-contrast` on purpose; token/APCA checks are `pnpm run test color-contrast` (in `test fast`). Archive “fix axe timing” items largely superseded unless re-enabling axe contrast is desired.
- **`test a11y` does not cover focus or keyboard behavior** — axe evaluates static markup: no tab order, no focus-visibility check, no focus management. Don’t claim keyboard coverage from a passing a11y run. Dedicated tooling **shipped 2026-08-15**: **`pnpm run focus-audit -- --base-url http://localhost:8080`** (`scripts/focus-audit/`, docs in **`docs/commands.md`** § Focus and Keyboard Audit). Needs a **served** site (`file://` fails — CSP + module loading) and takes **~10 min**; writes dated **EARL JSON-LD** + markdown into gitignored **`docs/designs/scratch/`**. Layout: portable **`collect.js`** / **`evaluate.js`** / **`rules.js`** / **`earl.js`** / **`report.js`** + site-specific **`jonplummer.config.js`** (the only file to swap for another site — `collect.js` must not require outside its directory). **`--seed`** reproduces the WCAG-EM random 10% sample. **`sanityOnly: true`** on **`/color/`** + **`/type/`** skips per-stop screenshots (control counts would dominate the run) — those pages get no automated focus-visibility evidence. Puppeteer has no combined **`Shift+Tab`**: use **`keyboard.down('Shift')`** / **`press('Tab')`** / **`up('Shift')`**. Skip links legitimately leave **`activeElement`** on **`<body>`** — assert with **`expectFocusWithin`** (where the next Tab lands), not **`expectFocus`**, or you get a false positive. Run via **`env -u PUPPETEER_CACHE_DIR`** like the OG scripts. Original spec: **`docs/designs/specs/2026-08-13-focus-keyboard-audit-design.md`**: portable Puppeteer collector + project config + evaluator, deliberately **outside** the test suite (infrequent, deliberate audit — not an authoring guard), rules tagged with WCAG success criteria so output can later feed a VPAT/ACR. **Don't invent formats for a11y results** — the standards exist: **ACT Rules** (`w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/act/rules/`, 6-char IDs, e.g. **`oj04fd`** defines focus-visible as ≥1 device pixel in the **viewport scrolling area** differing in **HSL** when focused, with a **1s dwell** before sampling); **EARL 1.0 as JSON-LD** (`w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/act/report/earl/` — `@context`/`@graph`, TestSubject + Assertion, outcomes `earl:passed|failed|inapplicable|cantTell|untested`, `mode: semiAuto`); **WCAG-EM 2.0** (sampling = structured + random 10% + complete processes); **ITI VPAT 2.5Rev** (Apr 2025; 508/EU/WCAG/INT editions; Supports / Partially Supports / Does Not Support / Not Applicable + Remarks). ACT rules are **informative, not normative** — all-passed maps to “needs further testing”, never “Supports”. Shipped 2026-08-16 from the first run: **`/color/`** + **`/type/`** home-preview facsimiles are **`inert`**; lightbox arrows use **`aria-disabled`** (not **`disabled`**); control focus is a shared ring (**`--focus-ring-color`** / **`--focus-ring-width`** / **`--focus-ring-offset`**, accent 2px / 2px offset) on **`button`**, **`select`**, **`input`**, **`textarea`**, **`summary`**, and the skip link — links stay accent recolor + underline. Content-warning `<details>` summary now has **`:focus-visible`** matching **`:hover`**. Hover-vs-focus audit rule is still a queued follow-up for catching the next case like that.
- **Do not rename `wisdom-entries.yaml` → `wisdom.yaml`** while `wisdom.js` exists — both would map to global `wisdom` and raw YAML overwrites built `entries`.
- **Wisdom entry slugs are optional** — `eleventy/utils/wisdom-build.js` derives stable hash-based ids from `body` when `slug` is missing, and `scripts/test/wisdom-yaml.js` only validates `slug` when provided.
- **Wisdom YAML can break when multiline markdown is serialized as plain inline `body:` strings** — keep wisdom `body` content in block scalar style (`|-`/`|`) when rewriting to avoid mapping/indentation parse errors. Block lines must be indented **more** than the `body:` line (e.g. two extra spaces); same indentation as `body:` is invalid YAML.
- **Shortcuts: Notes folder export** — Inside **Repeat with Each**, actions (e.g. **Make Markdown from Note**) must take **`Repeat Item`**, not the **Find Notes** output variable (often also labeled **Note**). Using the find output inside the loop triggers **Choose item** with **Done** disabled.
- **`mergePostsAndLinks` needs `pageNumber === 0` for “page 1” behavior** — only then does it prepend links dated after the newest post. `src/links-feed.njk` must pass `0` (e.g. `mergePostsAndLinks(links, 0)`); otherwise the feed drops newer links and looks frozen at the latest post date.
- **OG image generation** — Recurses `src/**/*.njk` (excludes `_posts`/`_includes`/`_data`/`assets`). Skips `pagination:` templates (one file → many URLs; use shared `ogImage` like `index.png`). `ogImage: auto` must not trigger perpetual regen: `needsRegeneration` ignores `auto` for path comparison. **Paths already in front matter skip shared-dep mtime regen** — style-token updates need **`pnpm run generate-og-images -- --force`**. Cursor may set **`PUPPETEER_CACHE_DIR`** to a sandbox path without Chrome; use **`env -u PUPPETEER_CACHE_DIR`** so Puppeteer finds `~/.cache/puppeteer`. Deploy OG line uses `filesUpdated` for “unchanged”; ℹ️ only when `ogImage` was absent in front matter but the PNG file already existed. **PNG basename rules**: **`scripts/utils/og-image-filename.js`** — for dated posts, use the source **`YYYY-MM-DD-*` filename** (not front-matter `Date` / UTC midnight ISO, which can shift the local day / double-prefix the slug). Guard: **`pnpm run test og-image-filename`** (in `test unit`). **`/ogimages/`** HTML preview hardcodes light tokens on **`.og-image-rendered`** (keep in sync with extract / `:root` light halves — e.g. content field `oklch(98%)`). Layout (2026-08): one-sheet soft field (no mat), top-aligned, **`--og-type-scale: 1.6`** on logotype/title/body/date from live tokens (**`--font-size-logotype` / `--font-size-2xl` / `--font-size-base`**), lockup→title **`--spacing-3xl`**. Same rules in **`og-image.njk`**. Preview HTML before full **`--force`** PNG regen. Grid sort: **`scripts/utils/og-image-gallery-sort.js`** uses front-matter **`date`**, then **`YYYY-MM-DD-`** parse from post-style filenames, then PNG **`mtime`**.
- **GitHub push + Dependabot `remote:` line** — On `git push`, GitHub may print `GitHub found N vulnerability…` with a Dependabot link. **Not controllable from this repo** (no git hook or config disables it). Security / Dependabot can already show **Fixed** while that line still appears until alerts are dismissed or GitHub rescans. **Agents**: after a successful push, do not repeat or escalate that footer as a new action item unless the user asks for a security review.
- **`@11ty/eleventy-plugin-rss` v3** — ESM-only (`export default`); `require("@11ty/eleventy-plugin-rss")` fails. Use `await import("@11ty/eleventy-plugin-rss")` and `addPlugin(rssModule.default)`; root `.eleventy.js` must be `async` and `await configurePlugins(...)`.
- **`@11ty/eleventy` 3.1.6** — Fixes Node 26 **DEP0205** (`module.register()` → `registerHooks()` in ESM resolver); bump from 3.1.5 when builds show that deprecation warning.
- **`cspell` 10.x** — Declares `engines.node: >=22.18.0`; root `package.json` includes matching `engines` so installs match spell tooling. `cspell.json` / `spell.js` unchanged for this bump.
- **`@xmldom/xmldom` 0.9.x** — Used only in `scripts/test/rss-feed.js` (`DOMParser`); `require()` still works; bump is `package.json` + lockfile.
- **RSS feed freshness** — `scripts/test/rss-feed.js` reports **>30 days** since newest item as **`addWarning`** (`rss-freshness`), not `addIssue`; test exits 0 with warnings only.
- **`markdownlint-cli2` 0.22.x** — Invoked from `scripts/test/markdown.js` with `.markdownlint.json`; 0.20→0.22 needed no config or script changes here.
- **Stale `_site/` paths** — After removing or renaming templates, Eleventy may not delete old HTML under `_site/`; SEO/OG tests then fail on orphans (e.g. former `_site/type/gallery/`). Remove the stale directory or wipe `_site` before `pnpm run test fast`. Production `eleventy` does **not** empty `_site/` first (`pnpm run clean` does; wiping also regenerates `_site/img/`).
- **`/NaN/NaN/NaN/` post permalinks** — `_posts.11tydata.js` falls back to `Date#getFullYear()` when the post date is invalid (file moved before it has `YYYY-MM-DD` in the name or front matter). `dev` watch writes `_site/NaN/…`; a later valid date does not delete it. RSS/sitemap are built from collections, not a `_site` walk, so they will not list the orphan once the source date is valid. IndexNow and rsync **do** walk leftover HTML — post-build tests (`og-images`, `seo`, `html`) are the gate that stops a dirty `_site` from deploying. `--delete` would remove a remote NaN path on a later clean deploy.
- **`links.yaml` nested quotes** — Double-quoted YAML: escape ASCII `"` as `\"`; curly `“`/`”` need no backslash (`\\“` leaves a visible `\`). Pattern: `"\"Outer quote with “inner curly” inside.\""`. Guard: `pnpm run test links` rejects `\` before curly quotes in descriptions.
- **Side project covers** — `coverImage` is the `/sides/` grid card only (`side_list_item.njk`, 16:9 crop + optional `coverPosition`/`coverZoom`). Detail-page screenshots are markdown in the project file (`![alt](/assets/images/…)`), same as portfolio posts — not a slot in `side_detail.njk`. `.side-detail` opted out of the article grid (links aside has no column), so those images stay reading-width and do not get portfolio full-bleed or lightbox unless a `*caption*` line makes a `<figure>`. Do not add a layout hero.

### What worked
- Parallel agents work well for independent code changes (e.g., two unrelated simplifications at once)
- modern-css.com is a good reference for identifying CSS modernization opportunities
